[
  {
    "comment_id": 4438769208,
    "path": "apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts",
    "line": 211,
    "finding": "👮 **Wachiman** · 🟠🐛 **Fix · bug: Every error in a group move is reported as \"stale\"**\n\nThe `catch` around `workspaceGate().run(...)` turns any thrown error into `refuseAll(\"stale\")`. Only a `StaleWorkspaceError` from the gate means that. Two other errors also land here:\n\n- `vaultActivity.run(\"library\", …)` calls `admit()`, which throws `MaintenanceError` (`vault-activity.ts:96`) when \"Check and fix files\" starts after the early `inMaintenance` check at line 161 but before the gate admits the call.\n- A rejected `loadDeviceId` throws too.\n\nIn both cases the user is told their window's workspace is no longer active, which is false.\n\nSuggested fix: map `StaleWorkspaceError` to \"stale\" and `MaintenanceError` to \"maintenance\". Map anything else to \"io\". This is the same mapping `runMoveGroup` already uses for an item that throws.\n\n<!-- wachi:finding -->",
    "replies": [
      {
        "author": "csdev19",
        "body": "> [!NOTE]\n> 🤖 **Claude Sonnet 5.5 responding on behalf of Cristian Sotomayor**\n\nFixed in fac69179: a thrown group move now maps `StaleWorkspaceError` to `stale`, `MaintenanceError` to `maintenance` and anything else to `io` (`refusalOfError`, with a unit test)."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "comment_id": 4438769214,
    "path": "apps/kaipu-record/src/main/workspaces/index.ts",
    "line": 171,
    "finding": "👮 **Wachiman** · 🟡🐛 **Consider · bug: A rejected device-id promise is cached for the rest of the process**\n\n`deviceId ??= loadDeviceId(...)` keeps the promise even when it rejects. After one failure, for example a transient read error in userData, every later group move rejects at `await deviceId` until the app restarts. With the catch below, the user also sees each of those as \"stale\". Consider resetting `deviceId = null` when the promise rejects.\n\n<!-- wachi:finding -->",
    "replies": [
      {
        "author": "csdev19",
        "body": "> [!NOTE]\n> 🤖 **Claude Sonnet 5.5 responding on behalf of Cristian Sotomayor**\n\nFixed in fac69179: a rejected `loadDeviceId` clears the cached promise, so the next group asks again."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "comment_id": 4438769220,
    "path": "apps/kaipu-record/src/shared/types/workspaces.ts",
    "line": 208,
    "finding": "👮 **Wachiman** · 🟠📝 **Fix · docs: `skipped` doc says whole-group refusals go there, but the code puts them in `failed`**\n\nThe comment on `skipped` says it also holds items from a group that \"was refused before it began\". But `moveItems` in `main/workspaces/index.ts:153-158` builds a whole-group refusal (`busy`, `stale`, `maintenance`) with every item in `failed` and `skipped: []`. Only Stop fills `skipped` (`move-group.ts:38`). Either change the comment, or have `refuseAll` fill `skipped` if that is the intended contract.\n\n<!-- wachi:finding -->",
    "replies": [
      {
        "author": "csdev19",
        "body": "> [!NOTE]\n> 🤖 **Claude Sonnet 5.5 responding on behalf of Cristian Sotomayor**\n\nFixed in fac69179: the comment on `skipped` now says only Stop fills it; a group refused as a whole lists every item in `failed` and leaves `skipped` empty. I kept the code's contract, because the renderer already counts `failed` for that case."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "comment_id": 4438769272,
    "path": "packages/i18n/messages/es.json",
    "line": 2623,
    "finding": "👮 **Wachiman** · 🟠🐛 **Fix · bug: Spanish move strings say \"workspace\" where the rest of the app says \"espacio de trabajo\"**\n\nThree new `move.*` strings leave the term in English: `chipLabel` (\"Mover a otro workspace\", line 2617), `newWorkspace` (\"Nuevo workspace…\", line 2623) and `reason_stale` (\"el workspace cambió\", line 2662). The existing Spanish strings for the same idea say \"espacio de trabajo\": `add` is \"Nuevo espacio de trabajo…\" (line 2562), and so are `addAction` and `newTitle` (lines 2588–2589), and `editNotWritable` uses it too. As a result, the switcher shows \"Nuevo espacio de trabajo…\" and the Move to menu shows \"Nuevo workspace…\" for the same action. Fix: use \"espacio de trabajo\" in all three strings.\n\n<!-- wachi:finding -->",
    "replies": [
      {
        "author": "csdev19",
        "body": "> [!NOTE]\n> 🤖 **Claude Sonnet 5.5 responding on behalf of Cristian Sotomayor**\n\nFixed in 180fd5d8: `chipLabel`, `newWorkspace` and `reason_stale` say \"espacio de trabajo\". (`locationParentMissing` still quotes the \"Default workspace\" name; that is the workspace's actual name, not the term.)"
      }
    ]
  }
]

